WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:06.230
- Illness is universal.

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:08.410
Access to care is not.

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:11.160
And realizing this lit a fire in my soul.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.540
No one should die
because they live too far

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.143
from a doctor or clinic.

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:19.360
I wish that you would help us recruit

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.050
the largest army of
community health workers

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:23.710
the world has ever known

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.540
by creating the Community Health Academy.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.763
A global platform to
train, connect and empower.

00:00:34.429 --> 00:00:36.540
(inquisitive music)

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.803
- They had a big idea to change the world.

00:00:40.047 --> 00:00:42.407
But they couldn't do it alone.

00:00:42.407 --> 00:00:43.737
- For my wish.

00:00:43.737 --> 00:00:44.570
- For my wish.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:45.495
- I wish.

00:00:45.495 --> 00:00:46.328
- So that my wish.

00:00:46.328 --> 00:00:48.411
- And now, here's my wish.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:01:01.590
- Epidemic diseases like Ebola, HIV, Zika,

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:04.100
emerge from remote, rural communities,

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:07.410
including the rainforests
of West and Central Africa.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.810
These are the hotspots of disease.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:11.630
They're the hotspots of infections.

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:14.269
They're the hotspots of
death that are located

00:01:14.269 --> 00:01:17.560
in the blind spots of
the global health system.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:19.670
The idea that disease anywhere

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:22.430
can be a threat to people
everywhere is very real.

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:24.460
So, how do we stop this?

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:27.440
Well, it's to enable
community health workers

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:30.580
to prevent, detect and
respond to outbreaks

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:31.843
at their very source.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:45.730
There are a billion people

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:48.140
who live in the world's
most remote communities

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.350
and while we've made great advances

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:53.596
in medicine and in technology,

00:01:53.596 --> 00:01:57.230
our innovations are not
reaching the last mile.

00:01:57.230 --> 00:02:00.373
They're not reaching
these remote communities.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:06.890
We launched a non-profit
called Last Mile Health

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:10.580
and Last Mile Health's mission is to bring

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:13.993
a healthcare worker within
reach of everyone, everywhere.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.030
A community health worker is someone

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:22.910
who lives in one of these communities

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:25.370
that's cut off several days away

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:27.370
from the nearest clinic and
they may not have had a chance

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:29.653
to finish even high school.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:34.430
They're trained to perform medical skills

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:36.173
that can save lives.

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:46.223
Their job is to go door to
door to provide healthcare.

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:57.080
- When I was little, I had a
passion to help communities.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:58.800
I loved taking care of children.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.653
So when the community
came here to find people,

00:03:02.653 --> 00:03:04.130
I put my hand up.

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:06.193
I said I wanted to help
the little children.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:11.030
- What these community health
workers like Serena are doing

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:13.640
is trying to bring the kind of healthcare

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:15.430
your family doctor may provide,

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:18.103
but in places your family
doctor may never go.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:30.080
- When I wake up in the morning,

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.313
put my bag on my back,

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:38.880
the distances that I walk

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:42.603
is sometimes two hours,
three hours in the forest.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:48.640
Some areas of creeks,
they join with the ocean,

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:50.823
so even crossing, you
find it so difficult.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:54.690
- Community health workers are trained

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:57.150
to address the health problems
of their own community.

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:59.070
In a country like Liberia,

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:03.893
it could mean helping a mother
get treatment for her child

00:04:03.893 --> 00:04:05.893
suffering from malaria.

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:17.560
- In Liberia, the children
die more than the others,

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:20.330
because we have, some
people in the villages,

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:22.130
they don't sleep under mosquito net.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:27.910
- We already know community health workers

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:30.830
can help healthcare
systems save more lives.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:33.110
Their ability to do that is strengthened

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:35.310
when they're enabled
with modern technology.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:43.653
If community health workers
were equipped with smart phones

00:04:43.653 --> 00:04:46.070
this would increase their ability

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:50.313
to prevent, detect, and respond
to outbreaks and epidemics.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:54.910
It's time for technology
to help reinvent healthcare

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:56.313
on a game-changing scale.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:01.960
We are building the world's
first education platform

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:04.700
for community health workers,

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:07.674
that allow them to see the condition.

00:05:07.674 --> 00:05:10.550
There's instruction on the
phone to help the worker

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:12.994
decide what treatment to give.

00:05:12.994 --> 00:05:17.994
But, equipping 50,000
community health workers

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:22.920
with smart phones is an
extraordinary, ambitious effort,

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:26.940
larger than what our
organization alone could take on.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:28.833
It required collaboration.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:37.290
We realize that working
together with other partners,

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:38.453
like Living Goods,

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:43.473
would help us truly solve that problem.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:49.910
And then, we learned about
The Audacious Project.

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:51.660
A new opportunity that TED

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.900
and a group of visionary philanthropists

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:57.500
had been working on, to fund

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:01.460
some of the boldest most
audacious ideas in the world.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:02.940
So that's all very exciting,

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:05.397
because many, many more millions
of children and families

00:06:05.397 --> 00:06:07.724
are now gonna have a chance at getting it,

00:06:07.724 --> 00:06:10.273
and they're gonna get it
from their own neighbors.

00:06:10.724 --> 00:06:14.000
- They say health workers for everyone, 
everywhere …

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:18.720
Community health workers
become the very people

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:21.003
who can make a difference.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:24.003
— I love children, and I love my community,
and my community love me. 

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:29.330
I have love and passion for the job, so 
I will continue to work for my people. 

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:32.680
We could, by 2030, save 30 million lives,

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:35.973
by training these workers
to do 30 services.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:40.820
We as people are not defined
by the conditions we face,

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:42.950
no matter how hopeless they seem.

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:45.440
We're defined by how we respond to them,

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:48.510
and our response has to demand

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:50.923
a health worker for everyone everywhere.

